{#- Listen2 2.0 draft: Voice Profile (Pace and Liveliness). Claims 11 to 14, plan section 5. Liveliness is
    named only: the fact sheet says it has not been evaluated, so the page says nothing about its effect. -#}
{% from "components/listen2-2/slots.njk" import screenSlot, confirm %}
    <!-- Voice Profile -->
    <section id="voice-profile" style="background: #131315; border-top: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-bottom: 1px solid #2A2A2D" aria-labelledby="l2-profile">
      <div style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 88px 24px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 56px; align-items: center">
        <div style="flex: 1 1 460px; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px">
          <div style="font-family: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #FF66C4">Voice Profile</div>
          <h2 id="l2-profile" style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px); line-height: 1.1; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em">Set each voice the way you like to hear it</h2>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.6; color: #D4D4D0">A voice that suits a novel can feel rushed in a contract. Each Listen2 voice now has its own Voice Profile, and Listen2 keeps your settings with that voice. Switch to another voice and it has its own, and switch back and yours are still there. The new voices start at a Pace of Normal and a Liveliness of Most lively, and you can change either one.</p>
          <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 16px">
            <div style="border: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-radius: 20px; padding: 22px; background: #0B0B0C; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
              <div style="font-family: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #A3A3A0">7 steps, plus Voice decides</div>
              <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700">Pace</h3>
              <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: #A3A3A0">A calmer pace for a contract, a quicker one for the news. Each step is faster than the one before, and the voice stays the same at every one. Pace is how fast the voice itself reads; the playback speed control still works on top of it.</p>
            </div>
            <div style="border: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-radius: 20px; padding: 22px; background: #0B0B0C; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
              <div style="font-family: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #A3A3A0">5 steps, plus one the voice chooses</div>
              <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700">Liveliness</h3>
              <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: #A3A3A0">The second setting in the profile. Try a step up or down on a page you know and keep whichever you like listening to.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: #A3A3A0">You can change both from the reader while you listen, and save a profile you like as a preset to use on another Listen2 voice.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="flex: 0 1 280px; margin: 0 auto; display: flex; justify-content: center">
          {{ screenSlot(listen2Voices.screens.voiceProfile, 260) }}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
